## The canonical data — a single source of truth

The shared data for this project lives at:

```
@@DATA_LOCATION@@
```

That path is outside the repo and is never committed. Each person sets
`@@DATA_ENV@@` to their own working folder inside it; `global/` is the sibling
everyone reads. If someone's copy is somewhere else — a different Dropbox mount
point, a different drive letter — they change the env var, not this file and not
a script.

`<data root>/global/` holds the core data everyone works from. One copy, shared,
read-only. `project/global/data_manifest.md` records for each file its hash, its
shape, who promoted it, and why it is trusted.

Build in your own tree; promote deliberately:

```bash
python3 tools/promote.py <path-to-your-built-file> --note "why this is trusted"
```

Never write into `global/` directly, and never promote something whose
justification you cannot state — that silently turns one person's build into
everyone's ground truth.

